// Micro-benchmark: what a `state` hit costs. 200 top-level declarations, each
// one a hit on every run after the first (the slot exists, so the init block
// is skipped). `petal bench` starts every run from an empty stack, so this is
// measured on a kept stack:
//
//   cd core && cargo run --release --example rerun_timing -- \
//     ../test/benchmarks/micro/state_hit_top.ptl \
//     ../test/benchmarks/micro/state_hit_fn.ptl \
//     ../test/benchmarks/micro/state_hit_none.ptl
//
// A run's time less an empty program's (about 2 µs), over 200, is the cost of
// one top-level hit; state_hit_fn.ptl's less state_hit_none.ptl's, over 200,
// is the cost of one hit inside a function.
// Figures are in docs/dev/performance.md (A state hit).

